WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Genes of the Original Sin</b>

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.790
It's happening!

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.400
Come to me, Ogre!

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.660
I'm right here!

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.440
Minami! Alma!

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.580
Please, Akira, put an end 
to this hopeless scenario.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:29.080
EX-ARM Number 00 Alpha's 
full networking capabilities unlocked!

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:32.680
<i>Shit!</i>

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.840
<i>Shit! Shit! Shit! Shit! Shit!</i>

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.490
<i>It's Ignis Type-03 EX...</i>

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.820
<i>Ogre's latest version!</i>

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.730
<i>You may look a little different,</i>

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:56.250
<i>but your face annoys me just the same, Alpha.</i>

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.770
"The same"?

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.180
You sure got that right, Beta.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.250
I fought you as Ogre that day, too.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:09.940
I tried to take you out 
before you ruined everything!

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.870
<i>But you lost, remember?</i>

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:31.980
Yeah, but I finally get my rematch!

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.450
<i>I'm convinced.</i>

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.970
<i>I'm stronger than I was back then.</i>

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:13.920
I'm gonna shove a new ending 
down your throat, Beta!

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.500
<i>Don't get ahead of yourself!</i>

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.640
<i>I'll slap you down myself!</i>

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.710
<i>Alpha!</i>

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.730
How is he generating
so much power at that size?

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.370
I'm gonna destroy you now!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.720
<i>Big words, little man.</i>

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.620
<i>You can't do whatever it takes, like I can!</i>

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.420
Kimura!

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.550
Take care of the squad for me!

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:02.220
You got it, bro!

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.490
Not so fast.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.470
They're in perfect sync.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.660
Alma and I will handle things here.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.610
Minami, Ygg, I leave Jinkoku-sha to you!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.970
Okay, but Soma's...

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.040
I knocked her out gently.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.370
What's about to happen 
will be too painful for her to take.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.080
Let's bounce!

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.590
You're dealing with me.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.550
Stupid machine!

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:56.120
<i>I'm not done yet! 
I have plenty of raw material!</i>

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.760
<i>I'm just getting started!</i>

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.440
What a sight.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.800
I've ascertained the EX-ARMs 
to be a gift from space.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:17.450
Weapons that invoke almost supernatural
abilities when connected to a life form.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:30.350
I'm sorry to make you keep me company, Alma.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:34.200
Don't be. I'm doing this because I want to.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.740
Let's win, then.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.740
Let's win, and go back home!

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.640
Yeah.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:53.240
Number 21's ability 
is to freeze air in place.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:56.120
It can use that power 
for both attack and defense.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.180
You handle Soma, Alma.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:01.300
Got it. I'm taking one of your weapons.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.630
<i>You little punks...</i>

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.130
<i>I'll teach you not to take me lightly!</i>

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.920
This ends here!

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.940
Okay, this should keep the geezer alive 
for the time being.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:27.140
But nobody can heal <i>her</i> wounds.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.390
We must escape this area as soon as possible.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.410
Yeah.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.340
I'm coming for you, Hayama Gaho.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.220
Let's finish this, Soma.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:59.550
Die, stupid puppet!

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:03.040
I'll stop your list of crimes 
from growing any further.

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:44.900
<i>He can use his power 
in only two places at once.</i>

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.760
<i>That's one.</i>

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:51.340
<i>And he'll use the other 
to make a landing pad.</i>

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:54.650
Just as predicted.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:00.120
How... You shouldn't be capable of this.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.990
I'm not who I used to be.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.420
You can't block this bullet.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.470
I'm not just a sacrificial pawn anymore.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.900
I wasn't ordered to do this. 
I was <i>asked</i> to.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:24.790
From now on, I'll fight for myself 
and the people I care about...

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.920
of my own free will!

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.750
What's she mean?

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:33.800
I realized something 
when I got rid of her brainwashing.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.890
The rule set that governs an android's actions, 
like absolute obedience to humans,

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:43.360
and the restrictions placed on her self-defense 
and computational abilities,

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:44.850
had all been overwritten.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.600
You mean Alma's...

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:50.900
All her mental and physical limiters 
have been removed.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:54.990
She can kill a person without being
ordered to... of her own free will.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:10:00.940
She has become the freest piece
of technology in human history!

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:09.610
Go ahead and shoot. I'll never give
in to a mere machine like you,

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:11.790
not even if it kills me.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:25.290
<i>That was artificial muscle 
exploding under too much stress.</i>

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:29.390
<i>He put his very life at risk there, 
because his whole exoframe could've exploded.</i>

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:33.140
<i>He's just as broken as the others.</i>

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.000
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.440
It's over, Soma.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:04.940
Kill me.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:07.470
I said, "Kill me"!

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:13.240
Your body is so damaged 
that it can't even keep you alive.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:16.430
You knew you wouldn't last three minutes 
out of the suit.

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:17.980
So why did you do this?

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:22.350
My thirst for revenge 
is the only humanity I have left!

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.950
If I lost it, I'd just be a machine!

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:29.000
Just shoot me now! Do it!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.140
Do I even need to?

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.420
Don't you pity me.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.720
I can't.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:40.250
I don't understand how you feel.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.170
That's fine.

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:45.430
I'd rather die than have a
machine sympathize with me.

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:52.100
I used to think I couldn't understand
people because I was a machine.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.580
But I was wrong, wasn't I?

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:59.610
Even if I were human, 
I still wouldn't understand.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:01.800
Because I'm not you.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:06.620
Having an almost human-like freedom 
made me finally see it.

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:10.630
How lonesome it can be to be untethered.

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:13.920
That is why one loves one's fellow man.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.320
That is why one seeks companionship.

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:23.510
And that solitude is what breeds resentment.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:28.760
If that resentment is what keeps you going,

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:31.430
there's nothing I can say.

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:33.620
Shoot me.

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:36.270
Enough talk.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:45.110
The flame of revenge has been burning me up 
from within since the day I lost it all.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.330
I cursed them all.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:51.960
The terrorists, this world,

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:55.240
and even my parents and sister!

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:00.620
Stop it!

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.040
I won't.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:05.610
Even if you are to pass away 
consumed by hatred,

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.470
I'm sure Minami would've embraced you 
as you are.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.000
Cut it out!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:17.020
I never asked for this!

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:29.140
I thought I'd forgotten the warmth 
of human touch a long time ago!

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:31.660
Happy birthday, Sis.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.660
It's a set.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.440
Thanks, Soma!

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:41.640
I'll keep this with me forever!

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:53.740
She shed a tear.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:14:00.810
This is all too much for Minami. 
No, for anyone.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:06.990
We'll leave the village 
and enter the tunnel to the mainland soon.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.020
<i>We'll play no further role in this.</i>

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:14.510
I fight to protect the people dear to me!

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:16.620
That's how it is, and how it's always been!

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:24.170
That's right. That emotion is proof 
that you are alive, Natsume Akira.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.130
This is the end!

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.230
<i>Hey, watch where you're shooting!</i>

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:46.650
We must retreat. Send a car.

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:56.100
The rest is up to Akira.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:12.830
After everything you've done, 
I won't let there be any doubts about the outcome.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:15.850
It's you or me! 
Only the victor shall survive!

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:28.440
Leave this to me and escape.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:30.780
Get going!

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:33.050
No, I must end him.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:48.840
Hey!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.490
Bro?

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:58.420
"Bro"? Wait, Natsume Shuichi?!

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:05.260
Natsume Akira's elder brother, 
who worked on AI and android research at Iriya...

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:07.150
He's Auctioneer?!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:11.400
I thought he went missing 
after the Tokyo Attack!

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:21.400
You look like my brother, 
but you're not him, right?

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:25.030
Yes, that's right.

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:30.260
I'm a clone that Natsume Shuichi built, 
knowing he would die.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:32.730
A clone?

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:44.190
He made me to atone for the sin 
of being involved in the creation of Beta.

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:47.190
He... created Beta?!

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:51.670
Of all the foolish...

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:55.430
It all started sixteen years ago.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:05.670
An unforeseen accident took Akira's life.

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:10.040
Come with me, Natsume.

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.980
Professor Iriya?

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.750
This is an EX-ARM. Ever heard of it?

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:24.040
I've ascertained them 
to be a gift from space.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:31.340
Weapons that invoke almost supernatural
abilities when connected to a life form.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:39.350
They're fitted with technology far beyond
the capabilities of modern science.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.680
What is that?

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:48.370
It's your brother's brain inside this thing.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:53.850
This particular EX-ARM is activated 
by placing a human brain in it.

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:55.480
No...

00:17:56.040 --> 00:18:01.180
Your brother can live on 
connected to this EX-ARM.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:02.970
Not like this!

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.480
If we can unravel the mysteries 
of the EX-ARMs,

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:11.930
your brother will have contributed greatly 
to the advancement of science.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:17.060
How do you choose to use his life?

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:21.990
As a scientist, what can you do for him?

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:26.890
What <i>can</i> I do for Akira?

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:30.840
His brain's still functioning. 
All he needs is a body.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.040
I can build an android body for Akira!

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:50.440
I wonder how the immense power 
of EX-ARMs will change mankind.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:56.220
Just as mankind finds ways 
to use tools to its benefit,

00:18:56.220 --> 00:19:01.280
it also finds ways to use them 
to its detriment.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:04.820
Let us begin.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:22.710
Akira!

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:36.620
<i>Fitted with the brain of Natsume Akira, 
a human highly synchronized with tech,</i>

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:39.800
<i>we have EX-ARM Number 00 Alpha.</i>

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:42.760
<i>The other Number 00, Beta,</i>

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:47.000
<i>will be injected with this other matter 
brought in with the EX-ARMs.</i>

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:56.150
<i>The birth of Beta will make the essence 
of humanity clear for all to see.</i>

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.090
I see! So that is your answer!

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:33.280
"The essence of humanity"? 
It is our wills.

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:37.210
We don't let power consume us. 
We control it.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.960
Bro!

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:49.120
Even after I'm gone, my will shall live on!

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:52.010
It'll live on within you, Akira!

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:56.780
Bro...

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:02.400
I swore to myself, as a human being,

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:07.160
that I would do everything in my power 
to be the gatekeeper of EX-ARMs.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.130
I'm not letting you kill him again!

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:24.420
<i>Looks like you've finally 
remembered everything, Alpha!</i>

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:29.800
The more memories I recover, 
the more I'm convinced...

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:35.770
Beta, you can't be allowed 
to exist in this world!

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.260
I have a plan.

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:46.120
I trust your mind is made up, Akira.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:52.090
Yeah. I'm gonna put my best foot 
forward this time!

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.970
What does that crybaby idiot 
think he's doing?

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:32.250
How is he going to fight that monster?

00:23:32.250 --> 00:23:35.890
Next time, on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 011 - Proof of Humanity."

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Proof of Humanity</b>

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:38.920
You better come back to us, Akira!
